    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We observe that the results of Theorems 1.3 and 1.4 are inﬂuenced by β, even though the weights dβ ∈ A2 for all β ∈ (−1, 1). This demonstrates that the regularity of the solution to (1.2) is not solely dependent on the Muckenhoupt class, but rather on the explicit structure of the weight. Lastly, we note that our results extend to more general weights w that behave similarly near the boundary (see Remark 3.1)."
  }, {
